{"parentUuid":"6033f999-5369-4dcf-8764-a3232410a0c4","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a007c0e7513c91e75","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Uapwx4vdxYavN2o3T1Vi5c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01YXRvXgSBXC1uuua2pxJPrw","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"treewidth grid graph placement problem fixed parameter tractable"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8697,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":185,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8697},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":185,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8697,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8697,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozZLbSZSLnmSsxdQNQ7","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"d497da9a-55d5-401b-a21e-30869c739815","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:17.441Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6033f999-5369-4dcf-8764-a3232410a0c4","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a007c0e7513c91e75","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VWtap5jAmUdQ7RMfycRyvb","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"parameterized complexity 2D packing FPT algorithms 2024 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"FPT algorithms over linear delta-matroids with applications\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2502.13654\"},{\"title\":\"An ETH-Tight FPT Algorithm for Rejection-Proof Set Packing with Applications to Kidney Exchange\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.IPEC.2025.9\"},{\"title\":\"Parameterized Complexity of Path Set Packing | Algorithmica | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00453-025-01329-5\"},{\"title\":\"Welcome - Parameterized Complexity\",\"url\":\"http://fpt.wikidot.com/\"},{\"title\":\"[2509.11965] An ETH-Tight FPT Algorithm for Rejection-Proof Set Packing with Applications to Kidney Exchange\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2509.11965\"},{\"title\":\"FPT algorithms for packing k-safe spanning rooted sub(di)graphs - LIRMM - Laboratoire d’Informatique, de Robotique et de Microélectronique de Montpellier\",\"url\":\"https://hal-lirmm.ccsd.cnrs.fr/lirmm-04352990\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient Parameterized Approximation | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-032-11835-6_25\"},{\"title\":\"The Parameterized Complexity of Cycle Packing: Indifference is Not an Issue | Algorithmica | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00453-019-00599-0\"},{\"title\":\"[2502.13654] FPT algorithms over linear delta-matroids with applications\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2502.13654\"},{\"title\":\"On the Parameterized Complexity of Motion Planning for Rectangular Robots\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2024.65\"}]\n\nI've completed a web search for \"parameterized complexity 2D packing FPT algorithms 2024 2025\". Here are the key findings:\n\n## Recent FPT Results on Packing Problems (2024-2025)\n\n**Set Packing and Delta-Matroids:**\nRecent work investigates parameterized complexity aspects of problems defined over linear delta-matroids, with research on delta-matroid intersection and packing problems. Finding a set packing of size k feasible in a linear delta-matroid is FPT when parameterized by the rank parameter r.\n\n**Rejection-Proof Set Packing (2025):**\nA study of the parameterized complexity of a multi-agent variant of the Kidney Exchange problem explores whether a directed graph contains a packing of vertex-disjoint cycles, each of length ≤ d, covering at least k vertices. The work provides a kernel that is polynomial in k for constant values of d, and an ETH-tight FPT algorithm.\n\n**Path Set Packing (2025):**\nRecent research presents an FPT algorithm for Path Set Packing parameterized by feedback vertex number plus maximum degree, with results published in Algorithmica in 2025.\n\n**Motion Planning for 2D Robots (2024):**\nA study on the Parameterized Complexity of Motion Planning for Rectangular Robots (SoCG 2024) addresses translating k axis-aligned rectangular robots from initial to final positions without collision.\n\nThe search results show active research in parameterized complexity for various packing problems, though most focus on graph-theoretic packing rather than geometric 2D rectangle packing specifically.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"0651400d-2ee3-4b7f-9b7c-208af8af6bc4","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:23.871Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6033f999-5369-4dcf-8764-a3232410a0c4","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"d497da9a-55d5-401b-a21e-30869c739815","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a007c0e7513c91e75","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YXRvXgSBXC1uuua2pxJPrw","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"treewidth grid graph placement problem fixed parameter tractable\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Parameterized Algorithms for Power Edge Set and Zero Forcing Set | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-031-98740-3_25\"},{\"title\":\"Extending Orthogonal Planar Graph Drawings Is Fixed-Parameter Tractable\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2023.18\"},{\"title\":\"Large-treewidth graph decompositions and applications\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/2488608.2488645\"},{\"title\":\"Fixed-Parameter Tractability of Treewidth and Pathwidth | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/262282411_Fixed-Parameter_Tractability_of_Treewidth_and_Pathwidth\"},{\"title\":\"On Fixed-Parameter Tractability of Weighted 0-1 Timed Matching\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2508.10562\"},{\"title\":\"Large-Treewidth Graph Decompositions and Applications∗ Chandra Chekuri†\",\"url\":\"https://home.ttic.edu/~cjulia/papers/treewidth-decomposition-full.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Fixed Parameter Algorithms D´aniel Marx Tel Aviv University, Israel\",\"url\":\"http://cs.bme.hu/~dmarx/papers/marx-warsaw-fpt2\"},{\"title\":\"Fixed-Parameter Tractability of Graph Isomorphism in Graphs\",\"url\":\"https://par.nsf.gov/servlets/purl/10477129\"},{\"title\":\"Fixed-parameter tractable canonization and isomorphism test\",\"url\":\"https://sites.cs.ucsb.edu/~daniello/papers/tw-iso.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Fixed-Parameter Tractable Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/fixed-parameter-tractable-algorithms\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found several relevant topics related to your query about treewidth, grid graphs, placement problems, and fixed parameter tractability:\n\n## Key Findings:\n\n**Treewidth and Fixed-Parameter Tractability:**\nTreewidth is of interest to computer scientists as many NP-hard graph problems become fixed-parameter tractable on graphs with bounded treewidth.\n\n**Grid Minors and Treewidth:**\nThe results discuss the relationship between treewidth and grid graph structure. Robertson et al. observed that for a graph to contain a g × g grid as a minor, its treewidth may need to be as large as Ω(g² log g). Additionally, if a graph has treewidth at least some value g(k) = 2^(mO(k)), then it contains a grid minor of size k(2m)^(2k-1) × k(2m)^(2k-1).\n\n**Graph Placement and Drawing:**\nOne relevant result concerns orthogonal planar graph drawings being fixed-parameter tractable, and orthogonal planarity testing of bounded treewidth graphs.\n\n**General FPT Framework:**\nThis leads to substantially improved parameters in some Erdős-Pósa-type results, and faster algorithms for a class of fixed-parameter tractable problems.\n\nThe search results contain academic work on parameterized complexity, graph decompositions, and their applications to various algorithmic problems, though I didn't find a specific paper exclusively focused on a \"grid graph placement problem\" parameterized by treewidth.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"99c08886-c951-4981-8179-b7fcf0874a5a","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:24.839Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d497da9a-55d5-401b-a21e-30869c739815","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
