{"parentUuid":"cb78c483-3aff-40f8-970d-f06b06767d6f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a007c0e7513c91e75","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lk3JvZQJNzrRfxfmdZVxdH","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"rectangle packing parameterized number distinct sizes EPTAS FPT\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Bin Packing Problem - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/bin-packing-problem\"},{\"title\":\"Parameterized complexity and approximation algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://people.csail.mit.edu/rrw/presentations/marx-approx.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"EPTAS for the dual of splittable bin packing with cardinality constraint - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/abs/pii/S0304397523005157\"},{\"title\":\"FPT Approximations for Packing and Covering Problems ...\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol284-fsttcs2023/LIPIcs.FSTTCS.2023.28/LIPIcs.FSTTCS.2023.28.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"CMPUT 675: Approximation Algorithms Fall 2014 Lecture 8 (Sep 19): Bin Packing\",\"url\":\"https://webdocs.cs.ualberta.ca/~zacharyf/courses/approx_2014/notes/sep19-675.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Bin packing problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bin_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Parameterized counting matching and packing: A family of hard problems that admit FPTRAS - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0304397517306849\"},{\"title\":\"Packing Cycles Faster Than Erdős-Pósa\",\"url\":\"https://sites.cs.ucsb.edu/~daniello/papers/cyclePackingICALP17.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Faster Fixed-Parameter Tractable Algorithms for Matching and Packing Problems⋆\",\"url\":\"https://www.cs.mcgill.ca/~sue/papers/fpt-puzzles.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"algorithms Article A Survey on Approximation in Parameterized\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2006.04411\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query about rectangle packing with parameterized complexity, distinct sizes, EPTAS, and FPT. Here's a summary of the results:\n\nThe search returned several relevant sources discussing parameterized complexity and approximation algorithms, though most focus on bin packing and other related problems rather than rectangle packing specifically:\n\n**Key Findings:**\n\n1. **General Parameterized Complexity Framework**: Bin packing is fixed-parameter tractable (FPT) when parameterized by the number of item types and can be solved exactly using dynamic programming.\n\n2. **EPTAS Definition**: An EPTAS (efficient polynomial-time approximation scheme) computes a (1 + ε)-approximation in f(ε)n^O(1) time.\n\n3. **Hardness Results**: Geometric problems involving intersection graphs of rectangles, line segments and other objects arise in applications such as facility location, frequency assignment, and map labeling.\n\n4. **Related Work on Packing**: Recent work presents a PTAS for problems with constant values of parameters, with the time complexity being exponential in the parameter, while an EPTAS can be developed that need not assume the parameter is a constant.\n\nThe results provide context on parameterized complexity techniques applicable to packing problems, though the specific combination of rectangle packing with distinct sizes parameterized by the number of distinct sizes may require consulting more specialized academic literature.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ce132d4b-8d3c-4607-8565-05b17895a283","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:34.516Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"cb78c483-3aff-40f8-970d-f06b06767d6f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b18835d2-0866-4c55-9b2c-cbe71b8bf4f0","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a007c0e7513c91e75","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CqRKBfXg4594njuqxEoTrr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"strip packing\" OR \"bin packing\" parameterized complexity distinct item types 2024\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Polynomiality for Bin Packing with a Constant Number of Item Types\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/347577277_Polynomiality_for_Bin_Packing_with_a_Constant_Number_of_Item_Types\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Bin Packing with Fixed Number of Bins Revisited\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/221209347_Bin_Packing_with_Fixed_Number_of_Bins_Revisited\"},{\"title\":\"Approximation and online algorithms for multidimensional ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.csa.iisc.ac.in/~arindamkhan/papers/csrbinpacking.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Computational complexity analysis of set-bin-packing problem | IEEE Conference Publication | IEEE Xplore\",\"url\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/705257/\"},{\"title\":\"APPROXIMATION ALGORITHMS FOR MULTIDIMENSIONAL BIN PACKING A Thesis Presented to\",\"url\":\"https://aco.gatech.edu/sites/default/files/documents/khan_thesis.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Bin packing problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bin_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Parameterized complexity of configuration integer programs - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0167637721001565\"},{\"title\":\"Strip packing problem - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strip_packing_problem\"},{\"title\":\"Solving the parallel processor scheduling and bin packing problems with contiguity constraints: Mathematical models and computational studies - ScienceDirect\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0377221724007161\"},{\"title\":\"Bin Packing Problem - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/bin-packing-problem\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query about strip packing and bin packing with parameterized complexity and distinct item types from 2024. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Recent Parameterized Complexity Results\n\nStrip packing has been proven to be W[1]-hard when parameterized by the height of the optimal packing.\n\nStudies on the parameterized complexity of Minimum Volume Packing and Strip Packing showed that 2-dimensional Volume Packing is in FPT, while Strip Packing is W[1]-hard even in two dimensions, though an FPT algorithm exists for a special case.\n\n## Bin Packing with Distinct Item Types\n\nBin packing with few different item sizes (using binary multiplicity encoding) can be solved in polynomial time, building on breakthrough results from Goemans and Rothvoß.\n\nIn the high-multiplicity encoding for bin packing problems, items are classified into types with multiplicities rather than listed individually, allowing the problem to be rephrased in terms of configurations.\n\n## 2024 Developments\n\nIn 2024, a lower bound on strip packing was improved by Hougardy and Zondervan.\n\nThe search results indicate that recent work has focused on understanding the hardness of these problems under various parameterizations, particularly relating to the number of distinct item types and optimization metrics like packing height.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ee4d5636-f053-4ced-8ce0-6126ffac158c","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:36.143Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b18835d2-0866-4c55-9b2c-cbe71b8bf4f0","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9e51929a-a132-401f-b313-85f7df216c0f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a007c0e7513c91e75","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01A18qitDX1rBLYX2n4vU7Jf","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"geometric packing kernelization ETH lower bound 2D rectangles\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"A framework for ETH-tight algorithms and lower bounds in geometric intersection graphs | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/325884765_A_framework_for_ETH-tight_algorithms_and_lower_bounds_in_geometric_intersection_graphs\"},{\"title\":\"[1812.03155] Kernelization of Packing Problems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.03155\"},{\"title\":\"Tight Kernel Bounds for Problems on Graphs with Small Degeneracy | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-40450-4_31\"},{\"title\":\"A lower bound for online rectangle packing | Journal of Combinatorial Optimization | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s10878-019-00423-z\"},{\"title\":\"Approximation Algorithms for Rectangle Packing Problems\",\"url\":\"https://people.idsia.ch/~ingala/papers/thesis_rectangle_packing.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Search CORE\",\"url\":\"https://core.ac.uk/search?q=Kernelization+Algorithms+for+Packing+Problems+Allowing+Overlaps.\"},{\"title\":\"[2302.09220] A Tight Lower Bound for Compact Set Packing\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.09220\"},{\"title\":\"A General Framework for Bounds for Higher-Dimensional ...\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/cs/0402044\"},{\"title\":\"Kernelization of Packing Problems\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1812.03155\"},{\"title\":\"[2603.12999] Tight (S)ETH-based Lower Bounds for Pseudopolynomial Algorithms for Bin Packing and Multi-Machine Scheduling\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.12999\"}]\n\nThe web search returned several relevant results about kernelization, packing problems, ETH lower bounds, and related topics. Here's what I found:\n\n## Key Results\n\nResearch on kernelization of packing problems has made progress on tight bounds by showing non-trivial kernels with O(k^2.5) edges for finding k vertex-disjoint paths of three edges each, and improving the straightforward O(k^{d+1}) kernel to a uniform polynomial kernel where the exponent is independent of k when paths have d edges each.\n\nA framework for proving kernelization lower bounds was developed by Bodlaender et al., Fortnow and Santhanam, and Dell and Van Melkebeek under the complexity-theoretic hypothesis that coNP is not contained in NP/poly, and under this hypothesis, tight lower bounds have been shown for kernelization of d-Set Matching and other packing problems.\n\nFor d-Set Matching, the bounds are tight: it does not have kernels with O(k^{d-ε}) edges for any ε>0 unless the hypothesis fails.\n\n## Geometric Problems and Strip Packing\n\nStrip packing is FPT with respect to the height of the strip plus the maximum of the dimensions of the packed rectangles, which was previously only known to be in XP.\n\n## Recent ETH-Based Lower Bounds\n\nRecent work has provided a simple proof of a tight lower bound of the parameterized compact set packing problem based on ETH.\n\nA tight ETH-based lower bound for Bin Packing has been proved, ruling out time 2^{o(n)} T^{o(k)}, answering an open problem.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"ae1127cb-3570-4337-9ba0-536907d27740","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:37.279Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9e51929a-a132-401f-b313-85f7df216c0f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
