{"parentUuid":"406fe45d-4fd3-4bf8-9a88-68866937c1d7","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a007c0e7513c91e75","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01WaCv1ytRCf5KeQauvRjbJm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WviC2zcxPhDMJ7mex2jFg1","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"\"few item types\" OR \"few distinct\" 2-dimensional packing FPT n^O(k) configuration LP"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4173,"cache_read_input_tokens":28750,"output_tokens":170,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4173},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":170,"cache_read_input_tokens":28750,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4173,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4173,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozcFUTL3TZSz3Qmaob5","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"a10d75a8-8411-462a-a8e0-182bf6f20985","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:25:56.964Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"406fe45d-4fd3-4bf8-9a88-68866937c1d7","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a007c0e7513c91e75","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B3nfBeYmpt999iKaFrCbRC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"SoCG 2024 motion planning rectangular robots parameterized complexity\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"On the Parameterized Complexity of Motion Planning for Rectangular Robots\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2024.65\"},{\"title\":\"[2402.17846] On the Parameterized Complexity of Motion Planning for Rectangular Robots\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.17846\"},{\"title\":\"On the Parameterized Complexity of Motion Planning for Rectangular Robots\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2402.17846\"},{\"title\":\"The Parameterized Complexity of Coordinated Motion Planning\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2023.28\"},{\"title\":\"A Minor-Testing Approach for Coordinated Motion Planning with Sliding Robots\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.44\"},{\"title\":\"Parameterized Algorithms for Coordinated Motion Planning: Minimizing Energy\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.ICALP.2024.53\"},{\"title\":\"DROPS - The Parameterized Complexity of Coordinated Motion Planning\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/opus/volltexte/2023/17878/\"},{\"title\":\"The Parameterized Complexity of Coordinated Motion Planning - Royal Holloway Research Portal\",\"url\":\"https://pure.royalholloway.ac.uk/en/publications/the-parameterized-complexity-of-coordinated-motion-planning\"},{\"title\":\"[2312.07144] The Parameterized Complexity of Coordinated Motion Planning\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.07144\"},{\"title\":\"Optimal Motion Planning for Two Square Robots in a Rectilinear Environment\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.5\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the SoCG 2024 paper on motion planning for rectangular robots with parameterized complexity analysis.\n\n## Paper Summary\n\nThe paper \"On the Parameterized Complexity of Motion Planning for Rectangular Robots\" was presented at the 40th International Symposium on Computational Geometry (SoCG 2024), authored by Iyad Kanj and Salman Parsa.\n\n### Research Focus\n\nThe paper studies computationally-hard fundamental motion planning problems where the goal is to translate k axis-aligned rectangular robots from their initial positions to their final positions without collision, and with the minimum number of translation moves. \n\nThe aim is to understand the interplay between the number of robots and the geometric complexity of the input instance measured by the input size, which is the number of bits needed to encode the coordinates of the rectangles' vertices.\n\n### Key Settings and Results\n\nThe work focuses on axis-aligned translations, and more generally, translations restricted to a given set of directions, and studies two settings where the robots move in the free plane, and where they are confined to a bounding box.\n\nThe authors obtain fixed-parameter tractable (FPT) algorithms parameterized by k for all the settings under consideration.\n\nThe paper was published in Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics (LIPIcs), Volume 293, pp. 65:1-65:15.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c9145603-326d-48ff-8885-a7ae65009de0","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:02.764Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"406fe45d-4fd3-4bf8-9a88-68866937c1d7","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"a10d75a8-8411-462a-a8e0-182bf6f20985","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"11f7002f-1250-416f-bd07-34f6030c1de7","agentId":"a007c0e7513c91e75","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WviC2zcxPhDMJ7mex2jFg1","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"\"few item types\" OR \"few distinct\" 2-dimensional packing FPT n^O(k) configuration LP\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Approximation and online algorithms for multidimensional ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.csa.iisc.ac.in/~arindamkhan/papers/csrbinpacking.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Exact Solution Techniques for Two-dimensional Cutting and Packing\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/am/pii/S0377221720306111\"},{\"title\":\"Positions and covering: A two-stage methodology to obtain optimal solutions for the 2d-bin packing problem | PLOS One\",\"url\":\"https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371%2Fjournal.pone.0229358\"},{\"title\":\"Geometry Meets Vectors: Approximation Algorithms for Multidimensional Packing\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol250-fsttcs2022/LIPIcs.FSTTCS.2022.23/LIPIcs.FSTTCS.2022.23.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Polynomiality for Bin Packing with a Constant Number of Item Types\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/250613759_Polynomiality_for_Bin_Packing_with_a_Constant_Number_of_Item_Types\"},{\"title\":\"Multidimensional Bin Packing and Other Related Problems: A Survey ∗\",\"url\":\"https://tetali.math.gatech.edu/PUBLIS/CKPT.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ON MULTIDIMENSIONAL PACKING PROBLEMS∗ CHANDRA CHEKURI† AND SANJEEV KHANNA‡\",\"url\":\"https://chekuri.cs.illinois.edu/papers/vector-sicomp.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Bin Packing Problem - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/bin-packing-problem\"},{\"title\":\"Bin packing: configuration LP - TheoremDep\",\"url\":\"https://sharmaeklavya2.github.io/theoremdep/nodes/packing/config-lp/config-lp.html\"},{\"title\":\"FPT Approximations for Packing and Covering Problems ...\",\"url\":\"https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol284-fsttcs2023/LIPIcs.FSTTCS.2023.28/LIPIcs.FSTTCS.2023.28.pdf\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, I found relevant information about 2-dimensional packing with few item types and FPT algorithms using configuration LPs. Here are the key findings:\n\nConfiguration LPs are used in packing problems where there is a variable for each possible way of feasibly packing a bin (called a configuration).\n\nFor the specific problem of bin packing with a limited number of item types and FPT complexity, the bin packing problem with d different item sizes and item multiplicities can be solved in polynomial time when d is constant.\n\nAdditionally, bin packing is in FPT, parameterized by the number of vertices of an underlying integer knapsack polytope. Furthermore, bin packing is well-studied when the number of bins is some fixed constant k, and if the sizes of the items are polynomially bounded integers, then the problem can be solved exactly using dynamic programming in n^O(k) time.\n\nFor 2-dimensional packing specifically, algorithms analyze the fractional structured configuration LP to solve these problems.\n\nThe search results indicate that the combination of \"few item types\" (or \"few distinct\" types) in 2-dimensional packing problems can be solved using FPT algorithms with running times like n^O(k), where k parameterizes the number of distinct item types, and these approaches commonly employ configuration LPs.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"be131ec3-d8b1-4169-aa74-1ebe0813f376","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:03.416Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a10d75a8-8411-462a-a8e0-182bf6f20985","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"be131ec3-d8b1-4169-aa74-1ebe0813f376","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a007c0e7513c91e75","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Dns6trKB565PJpwMAqrzrc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough information now. Let me synthesize the findings.\n\n---\n\n# FPT / Parameterized Complexity for 2D Placement / Packing — 2024-2026 调研\n\n## 核心发现（按重点排）\n\n### 1. Treewidth / pathwidth 在 placement 上\n\n70×70 grid 的 treewidth 正好就是 70（n×n grid 的 treewidth = min(n, m)）。**这直接判死了 treewidth 路线**：典型 treewidth-DP 是 2^O(tw) · poly(n) 或更糟，2^70 完全不可计算。\n\n更精细：Robertson-Seymour 定理给出 grid minor ↔ treewidth 之间是线性的（Chekuri-Chuzhoy 2014 证明），即\"如果 treewidth 大就一定含大 grid minor\"。我们的容器**就是** 70×70 grid，所以 **win/win 路线在第一步就走到坏的一边**。\n\nBidimensionality 框架（Demaine-Hajiaghayi）能给 EPTAS / 子指数 FPT，但**前提是 H-minor-free 图**（planar、bounded-genus）。70×70 grid 本身不是 H-minor-free（它含任意大的完整 minor 序列），所以这套也不适用。\n\n### 2. 2D packing 已知的 FPT 结果（2024-2026）\n\n- **Strip Packing**：2D 情形下，按\"高度 h\"参数化是 W[1]-hard（Jansen 等）；按\"高度 + 矩形最大边长\"参数化才是 FPT。我们的容器边 = 70，矩形最大边可能就是 70 → 参数本身是 70，FPT 退化成 EXP。\n- **Bin Packing with constant number of item types d**：Goemans-Rothvoß 给出多项式算法（item types 是常数）。我们 facility types 大概几十种，**这是少数可能可行的方向**。\n- **Motion Planning for k Rectangular Robots**（Kanj-Parsa, SoCG 2024）：按 k = 矩形数量参数化是 FPT。但是**translation 问题**，不是 placement。我们 326 个 mandatory 当 k 是不可行的。\n- **2D Volume Packing** 是 FPT，但 **Strip Packing in 2D 是 W[1]-hard**（这是 placement 本质难处的标志）。\n\n### 3. ETH / SETH 下界\n\n- Compact Set Packing 在 ETH 下有 tight 下界（arXiv 2302.09220，2024 ICALP 后续）。\n- Bin Packing 的 ETH-tight 下界 2^o(n)·T^o(k) 已被排除（arXiv 2603.12999）。\n- 这告诉我们：**期望\"按某个小 k 拿到 2^k·poly(n)\"在 packing 类问题里大多被 W[1]-hardness 堵死**。\n\n### 4. Kernelization\n\nKernelization for packing（arXiv 1812.03155）主要针对 **set packing / d-set matching**，不是几何 rectangle placement。geometric kernelization 几乎没有正面结果——几何坐标不能像图问题那样压缩。\n\n### 5. 我们问题哪些参数可能\"小\"\n\n| 参数 | 估计值 | 可行性 |\n|---|---|---|\n| treewidth | ~70 | ❌ 死 |\n| #facility types | ~10-20 | ⚠️ 唯一有戏 |\n| #mandatory clusters | 326 instances | ❌ 太大 |\n| ghost rectangle 边长 | 6-70 | ⚠️ 仅当 ≤6-7 |\n| solution structure parameter | 未知 | ❌ 没研究 |\n\n### 6. 唯一一条勉强值得看的路线\n\n**\"Bin packing with constant item types d\" 的思路移植**：把每种 facility type 当 item type，用 high-multiplicity encoding + configuration ILP。这能在 facility type 数 d 固定时给多项式算法（运行时间是 d-塔指数级的）。但是：\n- 我们有 ghost rectangle 的几何约束（不是单纯 bin packing）\n- max_lex(area, min_side) 不是标准 packing 目标\n- 实际 d ≈ 10-20 已经让 d 塔指数太大\n\n---\n\n## 是否任何 FPT 路线对我们 PoC 可行\n\n**不可行**。理由：\n\n1. 70×70 grid treewidth = 70，所有 treewidth-DP 路线 2^70 直接死。\n2. Bidimensionality 要 H-minor-free，grid 本身不满足。\n3. 2D Strip Packing 在最自然参数化下 W[1]-hard。\n4. 唯一像样的\"few item types\"思路在我们 d≈15+几何约束+lex 目标下，常数项被推到不实用。\n5. 几何 kernelization 没有正面结果。\n6. SoCG 2024 的 rectangular robot FPT 结果按 k=矩形数参数化，我们 k=326 直接出局。\n\n**结论**：FPT/参数化复杂性是漂亮的理论，但我们这个实例的所有\"看起来小\"的参数（70、326、ghost min_side ≥6、facility types）都不在 FPT 能给出实用 f(k) 的区间。**继续走 CP-SAT + Benders + warm-start + 启发式排序 才是正路**。FPT 文献能给的最大启发是 high-multiplicity encoding（按 facility type 聚合）和 configuration ILP 两个技术工具，可以作为 master model 编码的优化点借鉴，**但 FPT 本身不构成独立的求解路线，PoC 不值得投入**。\n\n---\n\nSources:\n- [On the Parameterized Complexity of Motion Planning for Rectangular Robots (SoCG 2024)](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2024.65)\n- [arXiv 2402.17846 - Motion Planning for Rectangular Robots](https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.17846)\n- [The Parameterized Complexity of Coordinated Motion Planning (SoCG 2023)](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2023.28)\n- [Optimal Motion Planning for Two Square Robots (SoCG 2025)](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.5)\n- [A Minor-Testing Approach for Coordinated Motion Planning (SoCG 2025)](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2025.44)\n- [Kernelization of Packing Problems (arXiv 1812.03155)](https://arxiv.org/abs/1812.03155)\n- [A Tight Lower Bound for Compact Set Packing (arXiv 2302.09220)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.09220)\n- [Tight (S)ETH-based Lower Bounds for Bin Packing (arXiv 2603.12999)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2603.12999)\n- [FPT Approximations for Packing and Covering (FSTTCS 2023)](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/storage/00lipics/lipics-vol284-fsttcs2023/LIPIcs.FSTTCS.2023.28/LIPIcs.FSTTCS.2023.28.pdf)\n- [Bidimensionality and EPTAS (arXiv 1005.5449)](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/1005.5449)\n- [Bidimensionality and Geometric Graphs](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1107.2221)\n- [Linearity of grid minors in treewidth (Combinatorica)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00493-008-2140-4)\n- [Largest empty rectangle - Wikipedia](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Largest_empty_rectangle)\n- [Polynomiality for Bin Packing with a Constant Number of Item Types](https://www.researchgate.net/publication/347577277_Polynomiality_for_Bin_Packing_with_a_Constant_Number_of_Item_Types)\n- [Constraint Satisfaction with Bounded Treewidth Revisited](https://www.ac.tuwien.ac.at/files/pub/SamerSzeider10a.pdf)\n- [Parametric Algorithm for Largest Empty Rectangle from Line Segments (IJFCS 2024)](https://www.worldscientific.com/doi/10.1142/S0129054124500175)\n- [An ETH-Tight FPT Algorithm for Rejection-Proof Set Packing (IPEC 2025)](https://drops.dagstuhl.de/entities/document/10.4230/LIPIcs.IPEC.2025.9)\n- [Parameterized Complexity of Path Set Packing (Algorithmica 2025)](https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s00453-025-01329-5)"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2830,"cache_read_input_tokens":32923,"output_tokens":3131,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2830},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":3131,"cache_read_input_tokens":32923,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2830,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2830,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaozdBsBwSwmnAq8JvTYX","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"8a801ce9-a95b-4865-bb98-1ac55ed08233","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:26:56.497Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
